UnitKeystore::constructor
├── When access router is invalid
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_InvalidAccessRouter
└── When called
    └── it should set the accessRouter address

UnitKeystore::initialize
├── When called on the implementation
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
├── When already initialized
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
└── When not initialized
    ├── It should initialize UUPS
    ├── It should initialize with correct liveness
    └── It should initialize with correct max size

UnitKeystore::setAuthPolicy
├── When authDigest is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When nullifyingKeyHash is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When caller already has an auth policy
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_AuthPolicyAlreadySet
├── When nullifyingKeyHash is zero
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_InvalidNullifyingKeyHash
├── Given keystore tree is at capacity
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_KeystoreTreeFull
└── When caller does not have an auth policy
    ├── It should insert the auth leaf into the keystore tree
    ├── It should update the root
    ├── It should store the nullifying key hash for caller
    ├── It should emit LeafInserted event
    └── It should emit AuthPolicySet event

UnitKeystore::setAuthPolicyWithSig
├── When the signature is not valid for the account
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_InvalidSignature
├── When the deadline has passed
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_SignatureExpired
├── When called exactly at the deadline
│   └── It should register the account at the exact deadline boundary
├── When authDigest is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When nullifyingKeyHash is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When the account already has an auth policy
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_AuthPolicyAlreadySet
├── When nullifyingKeyHash is zero
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_InvalidNullifyingKeyHash
├── Given keystore tree is at capacity
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_KeystoreTreeFull
├── When the account is an EIP-1271 contract wallet
│   └── It should register the account when the wallet validates the signature
└── When the signature is valid for the account
    ├── It should insert the auth leaf for the account not the caller
    ├── It should update the root
    ├── It should store the nullifying key hash for the account
    ├── It should emit LeafInserted event
    └── It should emit AuthPolicySet event with the account

UnitKeystore::initializeEIP712
├── When already initialized at version 2
│   └── It should revert with InvalidInitialization
└── When called on a version 1 proxy
    └── It should set the EIP-712 domain

UnitKeystore::updateAuthPolicy
├── When oldAuthDigest is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When updatedAuthDigest is out of scalar field
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_OutOfScalarField
├── When caller doesnt already have an auth policy
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_AuthPolicyNotSet
└── When caller already has an auth policy set
    ├── It should recompute the old auth leaf from msg.sender, _oldAuthDigest and nullifyingKey
    ├── It should insert the new auth leaf into the keystore tree
    ├── It should update the root
    ├── It should emit LeafUpdated event
    └── It should emit AuthPolicyUpdated event

UnitKeystore::setViewingKey
└── When called
    ├── It should set the viewing key
    └── It should emit ViewingKeySet with correct old and new keys

UnitKeystore::_authorizeUpgrade
├── When caller does not have UPGRADER_ROLE
│   └── It should revert with Keystore_Unauthorized
└── When caller has UPGRADER_ROLE
    └── It should not revert

UnitKeystore::setKeystoreRootLiveness
├── When caller does not have upgrader role
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── When caller has upgrader role
    ├── It should update the liveness value
    └── It should emit KeystoreRootLivenessUpdated

UnitKeystore::setMaxKeystoreTreeSize
├── When caller does not have upgrader role
│   └── It should revert with Permissioned_NotAuthorized
└── When caller has upgrader role
    ├── When new max size is less than or equal to current tree size
    │   └── It should revert with Keystore_InvalidMaxTreeSize
    └── When new max size is greater than current tree size
        ├── It should update the max size value
        └── It should emit MaxKeystoreTreeSizeUpdated

UnitKeystore::_updateRoot
├── Given old root is zero
│   ├── It should not stamp any previous roots
│   ├── It should set current root
│   └── It should emit RootSuperseded
└── Given old root is not zero
    ├── When new root is fresh
    │   ├── It should set old root validUntil to block timestamp plus keystoreRootLiveness
    │   ├── It should set current root
    │   └── It should emit RootSuperseded
    └── When new root was previously superseded
        ├── It should set old root validUntil to block timestamp plus keystoreRootLiveness
        ├── It should clear the stale previous roots entry
        ├── It should set current root
        └── It should emit RootSuperseded

UnitKeystore::isKnownRoot
├── When root is zero
│   └── It should return false
├── When root is current root
│   └── It should return true
├── Given root was superseded
│   ├── When before validUntil
│   │   └── It should return true
│   └── When at or after validUntil
│       └── It should return false
└── When root was never seen
    └── It should return false
